 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=N&cursor=C` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": C2}`: one page
+  of items ordered by `id`. `limit` is 1..100 (default 20); `cursor` is the opaque
+  `next_cursor` of the previous page, which is `null` on the last page. An invalid
+  `limit` or `cursor` gets 400.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
